<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-E.P. GRIND OUT 58 RUN LEAD OVER BOLAND.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-E.P. GRIND OUT 58 RUN LEAD OVER BOLAND.</headline>
<dateline>PAARL 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A grim but determined 131 run</p>
<p>seventh wicket partnership between Mark Rushmere and Grant</p>
<p>Morgan helped Eastern Province to a total of 262 on the second</p>
<p>day of their Supersport Series match against Boland in Paarl on</p>
<p>Sunday.</p>
<p>Replying to the home side's 204 all out, E.P. resumed their</p>
<p>first innings on 30 for four and were soon plunged into further</p>
<p>trouble by debutant seamer James Albanie who claimed two quick</p>
<p>wickets to leave the visitors on 81 for six.</p>
<p>Morgan and Rushmere then eschewed virtually all their</p>
<p>attacking shots in favour of cautious defence and the Boland</p>
<p>attack soon wilted under stifling, 40 degree sunshine.</p>
<p>Morgan's 64 runs lasted almost four hours while Rushmere's</p>
<p>unbeaten 89 spanned five and a half hours, 269 deliveries and</p>
<p>contained just three fours and one six.</p>
<p>Boland first innings 204 (Kenny Jackson 120)</p>
